From 5d80df734cec8b15d0c0edc360efc937a833d60a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <agent@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:37:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add B-class external Unit I2C models

Add controller-visible I2C slave models for the first B-class Unit batch:
dlight (BH1750), accel (ADXL345), 4relay (U097) and weight-i2c (U180).

- dlight: single-byte command machine (power/reset/continuous/one-time,
  MTreg sensitivity register), fixture illuminance converted only inside the
  conversion window to the two-byte big-endian raw the driver reads.
- accel: ADXL345 register pointer with explicit POWER_CTL/DATA_FORMAT bytes,
  fixture x/y/z bytes derived from g values, read-to-clear INT_SOURCE; DEVID
  is reserved because the executable driver never reads it and no datasheet
  value is claimed.
- 4relay: 0x10 mode and 0x11 relay+LED read-modify-write register, per-channel
  QOM levels in the official driver bit order (RELAY1=bit0, LED1=bit4); the
  product-page reverse bit order is recorded as a documented conflict.
- weight-i2c: fixture-derived 0x00 ADC, 0x10 f32 weight, 0x60 int32 weight*100,
  0x70 ASCII string, writable calibration/filter registers, 0xFE firmware and
  0xFF address. 0x60 semantic version remains unresolved and is documented.

These are transaction models, not electrical/mechanical/optical models and
they do not upgrade any runtime profile without guest evidence.
